  <static seed="1971" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/Percent/MTH20PercentOfNumberType3_10.pg">
    <statement><p><m>88\%</m> of <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> is <m>281.6</m>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>320</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 1</p>
<p>We will use proportion to solve this problem. Assume <m>88\%</m> of <m>x</m> is <m>281.6</m>, so <lq/><m>88</m> out of <m>100</m><rq/> corresponds to <lq/><m>281.6</m> out of <m>x</m><rq/>.</p>
<p>We will write and solve the proportion:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \frac{88}{100} \amp = \frac{281.6}{x} \\
   88x \amp = 100 \cdot 281.6 \\
   88x \amp = 28160 \\
   \frac{88x}{88} \amp = \frac{28160}{88} \\
   x \amp = 320
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p><m>88\%</m> of <m>320</m> is <m>281.6</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 2</p>
<p>We will use the percentage formula to solve this problem. This translation from English to math may help you remember the percentage formula.</p>
<p><m>2 \text{ is } 50\% \text{ of } 4 \iff 2 = 0.5 \cdot 4</m></p>
<p>The question is: <m>281.6</m> is <m>88\%</m> of what? Assume <m>281.6</m> is <m>88\%</m> of <m>x</m>. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}
        281.6  \amp  = 0.88 \cdot x \\
        \frac{281.6}{0.88} \amp  = \frac{0.88x}{0.88} \\
        320 \amp = x
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p><m>88\%</m> of <m>320</m> is <m>281.6</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 3</p>
<p>In the sentence <lq/><m>88\%</m> of what is <m>281.6</m>,<rq/></p>
<p><ul label="disc">
<li>
<p><m>281.6</m> is the <alert>percentage</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>88\%</m> is the <alert>rate</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><lq/>what<rq/> is the <alert>base</alert> (following the word <lq/>of<rq/>).</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>By the formula <m>\text{base} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{rate}}</m>, we do a division to solve the problem:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{base} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{rate}} = \frac{281.6}{88\%} = \frac{281.6}{0.88} = 320 }</m></p>
<p><m>88\%</m> of <m>320</m> is <m>281.6</m>.</p>
</solution>
